0b4de52ae" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446568 1080 "I only" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446568 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446568 1083 #uuid "f3c44a28-6809-582c-b411-ffd64f99822a" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446555 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446556 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446559 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446562 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446566 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1077 "selection" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446555 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446569 1079 #uuid "9999ac46-6f4e-593f-907b-51eaf6bed9c7" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446560 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446561 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446563 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446564 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446567 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1077 "selection" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446560 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446570 1079 #uuid "b667cd59-08f8-5c6e-82c5-8b3ea70d6405" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446554 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446557 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446558 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446565 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446568 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1077 "selection" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446565 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446571 1079 #uuid "dfc4e87e-69ab-505e-8ac2-a813c8707da5" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446571 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1069 "q-131363" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1071 "![](images/5a/5ac051f640c2b4eae760eee9c567ec35ce3169384ec2305554e21c6d2d587bbe.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n\nIV. $F$ is irrotational" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1072 #uuid "322bc9a1-81a0-53ce-920d-1108825e3484" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446572 1074 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/80/80c67e624f960147b7980ee90700be800a414ab1e2a2e47faf7e8821ee0c0623.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446570 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1069 "q-105700" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1071 "![](images/18/183ea541b33b8389de46f9ee1560ed1da2b999191477d7490eb4970922bdc43c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $F$ is not irrotational\n\nIV. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1072 #uuid "40fa6adc-4679-5e13-a9fc-cb698f54e0e6" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446573 1074 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/b1/b1520791fcb3808604758b7d8f99443020d12075d4cc8bff78659880575b6ef2.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III and IV are false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational. And, since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446569 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1069 "q-126522" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(3x+2y)\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(-2,1).$" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1072 #uuid "aedf76f0-5451-58bc-9366-057502daac94" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true] [17592186446574 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x+2y) \\\\  & =-2x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(-2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(-2,1)} & =-2(-2)-2 \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534978 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1f352f1a-1af2-5144-a245-10854ead8b02" 17592186446554 "answer-20d194d4-bd3d-507f-8c59-044dbc7c81ea" 17592186446555 "answer-2afb3ad3-3542-5efb-92a8-0a844c4e01a3" 17592186446556 "answer-41e8b7d6-5c7a-5cf8-9c06-4d00a18513e2" 17592186446557 "answer-834c390d-d089-5913-89c4-08a44764f21a" 17592186446558 "answer-8854556c-9dbd-5890-ab92-8f478346b8b1" 17592186446559 "answer-8c74d4b9-7ed4-529a-b818-13e80317f0ae" 17592186446560 "answer-976ecb2e-4f04-5610-8207-c96b23772842" 17592186446561 "answer-98578e86-a0e6-513f-9db5-c6b91293012b" 17592186446562 "answer-b06370cf-7aa1-54f8-9e46-dc3a42a8d19d" 17592186446563 "answer-c7df0803-65d5-5e82-a045-a191ec18b671" 17592186446564 "answer-dcefe323-f572-5c28-853b-0586c0615884" 17592186446565 "answer-e0f07f8f-3a33-5658-92ff-2b538d7dcca1" 17592186446566 "answer-e214b4cf-1c30-5601-8ce0-ad80b4de52ae" 17592186446567 "answer-f3c44a28-6809-582c-b411-ffd64f99822a" 17592186446568 "answer-field-9999ac46-6f4e-593f-907b-51eaf6bed9c7" 17592186446569 "answer-field-b667cd59-08f8-5c6e-82c5-8b3ea70d6405" 17592186446570 "answer-field-dfc4e87e-69ab-505e-8ac2-a813c8707da5" 17592186446571 "question-322bc9a1-81a0-53ce-920d-1108825e3484" 17592186446572 "question-40fa6adc-4679-5e13-a9fc-cb698f54e0e6" 17592186446573 "question-aedf76f0-5451-58bc-9366-057502daac94" 17592186446574}}
